sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant K as Kernel
    participant I as /init (PID 1)
    participant R as Rescue console (TTY2)
    participant U as udev
    participant B as Network + SSH
    participant S as seatd
    participant C as Kiosk (TTY1)

    Note over K,C: 1. Early boot and rescue access
    K->>I: Start /init from the embedded initramfs
    I->>I: Mount /proc, /sys, /dev and /run
    I->>I: Connect console I/O and start timing log
    I->>R: Fork getty loop on TTY2
    Note over I,R: Ctrl+Alt+F2 - getty restarts after logout<br/>Password is configured later by background services

    Note over K,C: 2. Hardware discovery (foreground)
    I->>I: Load input, generic DRM and e1000 modules
    opt udevd executable exists
        I->>U: Start daemon and trigger subsystems and devices
        Note over K,U: Matching drivers load via udev<br/>Intel i915 and Realtek firmware available in initramfs
        I->>U: Wait for device events (maximum 10 s)
        alt Events settled
            U-->>I: Continue
        else Settle failed or timed out
            I->>I: Log warning and continue without readiness guarantee
        end
    end
    Note over I,U: Missing udevd or daemon/trigger failure is logged
    I->>I: Mount devpts, /dev/shm, /tmp and cgroup2
    I->>I: Enable loopback and run ldconfig or repair library symlinks

    Note over K,C: 3. Background services and graphics run independently
    I->>B: Fork background setup
    par Network and SSH setup
        alt eth0 exists
            B->>B: Bring link up and run DHCP (maximum 10 s)
            opt DHCP fails
                B->>B: Apply QEMU fallback IP 10.0.2.15/24
            end
        else eth0 missing
            B->>B: Report missing interface
        end
        B->>B: Configure root password (alpine)
        B->>B: Prepare SSH config and missing host keys
        B->>B: Start sshd in background if available
    and Kiosk setup
        I->>I: Prepare XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
        I->>S: Start seatd with output in /run/seatd.log
        I->>I: Wait for seatd socket (maximum 5 s)
        I->>I: Write /run/start-kiosk.sh
        alt seatd socket exists
            I->>C: Fork launcher: openvt -c 1 -s -w
            C->>C: Set environment and run Cage + Tauri
            Note over C: Output goes to /run/kiosk.log
            opt Graphical session exits
                C->>C: Record exit status in timing log
                C->>C: Show exit status and last 40 log lines on TTY1
                Note over R,C: No automatic kiosk restart<br/>Rescue console remains available
            end
        else seatd socket missing
            I->>I: Report error and skip kiosk launch
            Note over I,S: Show seatd log and rescue-console instructions
        end
    end

    Note over K,C: 4. PID 1 remains active
    I->>I: Wait for background children and collect exited processes
    Note over I,C: Boot milestones: local console + /run/boot-timing.log<br/>Launcher exit is reported separately from the Cage exit status